            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "晚点 — wǎndiǎn — \"to run behind schedule; to be late (of a train or plane)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "火车晚点了半个小时 huǒchē wǎndiǎn le bàn ge xiǎoshí — The train was half an hour late."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two third tones: wǎndiǎn is said wándiǎn, the first rising."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "晚点 (wǎndiǎn) is built from 晚 and 点, both inherited from Middle Chinese, mjonX and temX (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), glossed 'dusk' and 'a dot'. Late against the hour is the sense of the pair, which the dictionary does not give."
            }
          ]
        },
